          "label": "<p>Which national health programme in India employs DOTS therapy and GeneXpert test</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which national health programme in India employs DOTS therapy and GeneXpert testing, with a stated target of eliminating its target disease by 2025?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>National Vector Borne Disease Control Programme (NVBDCP)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NVBDCP covers malaria, dengue, chikungunya, filariasis, kala-azar, and Japanese encephalitis through vector control and treatment — it does not use DOTS.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>National AIDS Control Programme (NACP)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NACP provides free antiretroviral therapy, counselling and testing centres (ICTCs), and prevention of parent-to-child transmission for HIV/AIDS — not DOTS therapy.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ni-kshay (Revised National TB Control Programme)</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Ni-kshay employs DOTS therapy, GeneXpert for rapid diagnosis, and the Nikshay Poshan Yojana for nutritional support, with an ambitious target of TB elimination in India by 2025.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Integrated Disease Surveillance Programme (IDSP)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>IDSP coordinates surveillance for emerging infections across all states and union territories. It is a surveillance network, not a treatment programme.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The correct answer is Ni-kshay, the Revised National TB Control Programme. It uniquely combines DOTS therapy with GeneXpert testing and nutritional support, targeting TB elimination by 2025 — ahead of the global 2030 target."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. Ni-kshay is India's flagship TB elimination programme, combining the DOTS strategy with modern molecular diagnostics and nutritional support under Nikshay Poshan Yojana."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
